---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout 
  title="Experience"
  description="11+ years of professional experience as Technical Architect and Backend Engineer, leading distributed systems and microservices delivery."
>
  <div class="py-16 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-12">Professional Experience</h1>
        
        <div class="space-y-12">
          <!-- InTimeTec -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-accent-600 dark:border-accent-400 pl-6">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-start mb-4">
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">InTimeTec</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400">Technical Architect / Solutions Architect</p>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right">
                <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Aug 2023 – Present</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500">Jaipur / Client Engagements</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
              Lead solution architecture and hands-on delivery across concurrent enterprise and government platforms. Define system architecture, messaging topology, workflow orchestration, and technical strategy from RFP through production, while mentoring engineering teams.
            </p>
            
            <!-- Projects -->
            <div class="space-y-6 ml-4">
              <!-- Nebula -->
              <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/50 rounded-lg p-6">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-3">
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Nebula — Robotic Workflow & Mission Orchestration Platform</h3>
                  <span class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 whitespace-nowrap ml-4">Oct 2025 – Present</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 italic mb-3">
                  Event-driven robotic mission platform (n8n-style design/test/execute) across heterogeneous robot fleets
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                  <li>Architected distributed, event-driven microservices platform (NestJS, Kafka, RabbitMQ, Debezium, Redis, PostgreSQL, Flink, QuestDB, Temporal) for platform-wide robotic mission orchestration</li>
                  <li>Designed and delivered Mission Orchestrator: generic DAG execution with node-type dispatch, I/O propagation, and resilient error handling for multi-step mission design, test, and runtime</li>
                  <li>Established hybrid E2E testing (Jest, Docker Compose, Temporal) plus infrastructure probes for Kafka, Debezium, Redis, and RabbitMQ</li>
                  <li>Defined shared API contracts across services using OpenAPI/Orval and Zod</li>
                  <li>Delivered mission nodes including Robot.command (motion.navigate, compartment control, LiveKit camera streaming) and Sensor integration for KONE elevators</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              
              <!-- Al-Jouf -->
              <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/50 rounded-lg p-6">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-3">
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Strategic Office for Al-Jouf Region — Saudi Government Digital Platform</h3>
                  <span class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 whitespace-nowrap ml-4">Nov 2024 – Sept 2025</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 italic mb-3">
                  Monorepo digital government platform: bilingual citizen portal, e-services, CMS, identity — on-prem Kubernetes
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                  <li>Led solution architecture for monorepo digital-government platform (.NET microservices + Next.js) on on-prem Kubernetes</li>
                  <li>Delivered bilingual citizen portal and e-services with AR/EN RTL/LTR support targeting WCAG 2.1 AA</li>
                  <li>Integrated Camunda BPMN for e-service approvals, Orchard Core CMS, and Nafath + Keycloak identity</li>
                  <li>Platform covered search, notifications, reporting, audit, antivirus, and AI chatbot</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              
              <!-- Scenne -->
              <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/50 rounded-lg p-6">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-3">
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Scenne — Video-Sharing / Social MVP</h3>
                  <span class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 whitespace-nowrap ml-4">Jun 2024 – Oct 2024</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 italic mb-3">
                  Client engagement: Node.js, PostgreSQL, AWS S3, RabbitMQ, React Native
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                  <li>Architected and delivered video-sharing MVP with auth, social graph (follow/like/comment/share), and feed delivery</li>
                  <li>Implemented Redis feed/metadata caching and RabbitMQ for async orchestration</li>
                  <li>Enabled upload → FFmpeg compression → CDN playback path on AWS (S3, Lambda) with Docker/Kubernetes deployment</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              
              <!-- Blue Cross of Idaho -->
              <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/50 rounded-lg p-6">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-3">
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Blue Cross of Idaho (BCI) — Healthcare Data Pipeline</h3>
                  <span class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 whitespace-nowrap ml-4">Aug 2023 – Jun 2024</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 italic mb-3">
                  AWS Glue, Kafka MSK, Snowflake
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
                  <li>Designed enterprise clinical data pipeline ingesting CDEs/CCD/ADT into Snowflake via AWS Glue transforms and Kafka (MSK) streaming</li>
                  <li>Migrated legacy S3 data lake into structured Snowflake datasets for analytics-ready BI and reporting</li>
                  <li>Drove end-to-end delivery: requirements, architecture, API integration, CI/CD, and operational support</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <!-- Falabella -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 pl-6">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-start mb-4">
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Falabella</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Lead Software Engineer</p>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Jun 2022 – Jun 2023</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              <li>Led backend architecture on SODIMAC B2B e-commerce microservices (Node.js) enabling merchants to list and manage products for B2C channels</li>
              <li>Built React UIs on Flux-style state model and integrated Firestore for real-time sync</li>
              <li>Containerized services with Docker and contributed to CI/CD and performance hardening</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- EPAM Systems -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 pl-6">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-start mb-4">
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">EPAM Systems</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Lead Software Engineer</p>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Jul 2021 – Jun 2022</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              <li>Delivered CTC-CDS experience APIs for Cantire Corp's Core Digital Services / ODP platform on TypeScript, Node.js, Inversify, and Tsoa</li>
              <li>Owned microservice API modules consumed across e-commerce experience surfaces</li>
              <li>Collaborated with distributed teams to ship and harden CDS APIs used by multiple ODP modules</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- Scry Analytics -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 pl-6">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-start mb-4">
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Scry Analytics</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Senior Full-Stack Developer</p>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Feb 2019 – Jul 2021</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              <li>Built VoCP (Voice of Cancer Patients): Node-backed platform surfacing AI-generated insights and analytics from large-scale cancer-related conversations</li>
              <li>Delivered Collatio: document visualization and reconciliation (banking/gov docs) with Node.js, Angular, d3.js, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, Redis, and Docker</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- InTimeTec (Earlier) -->
          <div class="border-l-4 border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 pl-6">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-start mb-4">
              <div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">InTimeTec</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Senior Software Engineer</p>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Aug 2015 – Feb 2019</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              <li>Developed Cartos, a cloud fleet optimization/visualization platform for MPS providers (Node.js, Angular, Java Spring Boot, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, Redis, RabbitMQ)</li>
              <li>Built Portico on top of Cartos to integrate HP fleet tools (SOLD, Dart, etc.) with async messaging and search/cache layers</li>
              <li>Established early microservices + messaging patterns (RabbitMQ) and CI/CD practices</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-center">
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
            Interested in learning more about my experience?
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
            <a
              href="/nitesh-portfolio/resume"
              class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-accent-600 hover:bg-accent-700 text-white font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors"
            >
              View Full Resume
            </a>
            <a
              href="/nitesh-portfolio/contact"
              class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-200 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors"
            >
              Get in Touch
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
